• Revision checklist — I can explain the resting potential from permeability and the pump, quoting about −70 mV and the 3-to-2 ratio without hesitation.
• Revision checklist — I can narrate one action potential: stimulus, Na+ influx, reversal, K+ efflux, restoration, and the local currents that move it forward.
• Revision checklist — I can contrast continuous and saltatory conduction and explain, with node spacing, why myelin is both faster and cheaper.
• Revision checklist — I can write the five steps of chemical transmission in order and contrast the electrical synapse on proximity, speed and rarity.
• Revision checklist — I can map one signature job onto each of: cerebrum, thalamus, hypothalamus, limbic system, corpora quadrigemina, pons, cerebellum and medulla, and list the meninges outside-to-in.
• Revision checklist — I can trace a reflex arc’s five links with dorsal entry and ventral exit, and explain why the withdrawal beats the pain.
• Revision checklist — I can walk light from cornea to visual cortex and sound from pinna to auditory cortex, naming every relay, and state where impulses are actually generated in each sense.
• Revision checklist — I can separate crista from macula (rotation versus position) and rods from cones (dim versus colour) without cross-wiring either pair.
