• Revision checklist — I can walk through the pond: producers, consumers, decomposers, and the fixation–consumption–decomposition–reuse loop.
• Revision checklist — I can write NPP = GPP − R with every term defined, compute any term from the other two, and state the 170, 55 and 115 billion-ton figures.
• Revision checklist — I can recite the five decomposition steps in order, say what humus is, and predict rates from detritus chemistry and climate.
• Revision checklist — I can apply the two sunlight filters (under 50 per cent PAR; 2 to 10 per cent of PAR captured) and the ten per cent law to any chain.
• Revision checklist — I can distinguish GFC from DFC, assign levels T1 to T4, and define standing crop without confusing it with productivity.
• Revision checklist — I can explain the tree and sea pyramid puzzles, why energy never inverts, and the three pyramid limitations.
• Revision checklist — I can narrate hydrarch and xerarch stage by stage, name their pioneers, and explain the convergence on mesic forest and why secondary succession is faster.
• Revision checklist — I can contrast the carbon and phosphorus cycles: reservoirs, the 71 and 1 per cent figures, the 4 × 10^13 kg fixation, and the two NCERT differences.
• Revision checklist — I can quote the services ledger: 33 trillion dollars of services against 18 trillion of GNP, soil formation at about 50 per cent.
